{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And you forgot.</b> As though you forgot. He speaks in the holy spirit to his heart, that He is your Maker and has great power, for the heavens and the earth are in His dominion." "<b>Who oppresses.</b> As He said, \"I gave my back to those who strike\" (Isaiah 50:6)." "<b>To destroy.</b> To kill. And where now is the wrath of the oppressor?"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:00.053556602Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}